### E001

# Legal clearance for redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0) in the product

## Description
Resolves the gating legal unknown for the bundled object store strategy: whether MinIO, licensed AGPL-3.0, can be redistributed in the product's distribution model, and what derivative-work posture applies when the Platform Operator bundles and manages it. The documented decision determines which upstream is productized (MinIO, or the Apache-2.0 fallback) and unblocks all shipping work.

## Scope
- Obtain and document a legal determination on redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0) within the product's distribution model, including any conditions attached to clearance.
- Document the derivative-work posture for operator integration: whether bundling, deploying, and managing MinIO via the Platform Operator creates obligations beyond redistribution.
- Record a go/no-go decision per candidate store; on a no-go for MinIO, confirm (or reject with rationale) the Apache-2.0 fallback candidate named in the strategy (e.g., SeaweedFS).
- Communicate the outcome and selected upstream to all downstream teams.

## Acceptance Criteria
- A documented legal determination exists stating whether MinIO (AGPL-3.0) can be redistributed under the product's distribution model, including any conditions.
- The derivative-work posture for operator integration is documented.
- The decision names the upstream to be productized (MinIO or the fallback), or records that no candidate cleared review.
- Downstream teams can proceed without further legal interpretation of the AGPL question.

## HLR Traceability
- HLR-1 (P0): Legal review of redistributing the candidate object store, including derivative-work posture, completed and documented.

### E002

# Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store

## Description
Delivers the administrator-facing enablement of the supported, bundled S3-compatible object store through the Platform Operator, with productized images and a managed upgrade lifecycle, for disconnected and PoC clusters.

## Scope
- Add an enablement path in the Platform Operator for the bundled S3-compatible store: administrators can turn it on through operator configuration without external network access.
- Deploy and manage the store using the productized store image, referenced by pinned digest (the digest is filled in at execution time once the productized image is published — it is a configuration reference, not a build dependency).
- Manage the upgrade lifecycle: platform upgrades do not orphan or break an enabled bundled store.
- Provide a disable path: administrators can turn the bundled store off and fall back to customer-provided storage configuration.

## Acceptance Criteria
- On a disconnected cluster, an administrator can enable the bundled S3-compatible store through Platform Operator configuration with no external network access required.
- The enabled store runs the productized image referenced by a pinned digest, and the digest is available at execution time.
- A platform upgrade of a cluster with the bundled store enabled completes without breaking the store or requiring manual reconfiguration.
- Administrators can disable the bundled store; components fall back to customer-provided storage configuration without data-loss claims beyond documented behavior.
- Rollback/disable behavior is verified against the ad-hoc upstream MinIO installs it replaces (supported replacement for the unsupported field workaround).

