## Description

Makes Data Science Pipelines target the bundled S3-compatible store by default
when it is enabled through the Platform Operator, so pipeline artifact storage
works on disconnected clusters without manual endpoint configuration.

## Scope

- Default the pipelines artifact-storage connection to the bundled store when the
  store is enabled by the Platform Operator, requiring no manual endpoint or
  credential configuration.
- Preserve manual overrides: explicitly configured customer-provided storage
  continues to take precedence over the bundled default (connected environments
  are unchanged — replacing customer-provided S3 there is out of scope).
- Align with the Data Science Pipelines architecture context: the component
  already depends on S3-compatible object storage for artifacts; this work only
  changes default targeting, not the storage interface.

## Acceptance Criteria

- On a cluster with the bundled store enabled, creating a new pipelines
  application requires no manual storage endpoint configuration and defaults to
  the bundled store.
- Explicitly configured customer-provided storage continues to be honored (no
  regression for connected environments).
- Pipeline runs complete with artifacts stored in the bundled store on a
  disconnected cluster.

## HLR Traceability

- HLR-3 (P1): Data Science Pipelines connection defaults can target the bundled
  store without manual endpoint configuration.
