25	# Legal clearance for redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0) in the product
26	
27	## Description
28	
29	Resolves the gating legal unknown of this strategy: whether MinIO, licensed
30	AGPL-3.0, can be redistributed in the product's distribution model, and what
31	derivative-work posture applies when the Platform Operator bundles, deploys, and
32	manages it. The documented decision determines which upstream is productized
33	(MinIO, or the Apache-2.0 fallback named in the strategy) and unblocks all
34	shipping work, which the strategy explicitly holds back until clearance.
35	
36	## Scope
37	
38	- Obtain and document a legal determination on redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0)
39	  under the product's distribution model, including any conditions attached to
40	  clearance.
41	- Document the derivative-work posture for operator integration: whether
42	  bundling, deploying, and managing MinIO through the Platform Operator creates
43	  obligations beyond plain redistribution.
44	- Record a go/no-go per candidate store; on a no-go for MinIO, confirm (or reject
45	  with rationale) the Apache-2.0 fallback candidate (e.g. SeaweedFS) named in the
46	  strategy's open question.
47	- Communicate the outcome and the selected upstream to all downstream teams.
48	
49	## Acceptance Criteria
50	
51	- A documented legal determination exists stating whether MinIO (AGPL-3.0) can be
52	  redistributed under the product's distribution model, including any conditions
53	  attached.
54	- The derivative-work posture for operator integration is documented.
55	- The decision names the upstream to be productized (MinIO or the fallback), or
56	  records that no candidate cleared review.
57	- Downstream teams can proceed without further legal interpretation of the AGPL
58	  question.
59	
60	## HLR Traceability
61	
62	- HLR-1 (P0): legal review of redistributing the candidate object store (MinIO,
63	  AGPL-3.0) completed and documented, including the derivative-work posture for
64	  operator integration.
