33	# Midstream repo onboarding for the Apache-2.0 fallback object store
34	
35	## Description
36	
37	Creates the midstream repository for the Apache-2.0 licensed fallback object
38	store under opendatahub-io so a productized, supported store image can be built
39	from source. Executed only if the legal clearance denies AGPL-3.0 redistribution
40	for MinIO; per the strategy's open question, this restarts image productization
41	with the fallback upstream. The clearance decision names the specific fallback
42	upstream to productize; this epic validates that named candidate's S3
43	compatibility and onboards it. If MinIO is cleared instead, the MinIO branch
44	replaces this work.
45	
46	## Scope
47	
48	- Validate the S3 compatibility of the fallback upstream named by the legal
49	  clearance decision against the platform's needs (the Pipelines and model
50	  serving S3 workloads), and document the validation results. Escalate any gap
51	  that would disqualify the named candidate back to the clearance decision
52	  rather than substituting a different upstream here.
53	- Create the midstream repository for the named fallback store under
54	  opendatahub-io, mirroring the selected upstream version.
55	- Establish branching and versioning conventions consistent with other midstream
56	  components.
57	
58	## Acceptance Criteria
59	
60	- The S3 compatibility of the named fallback upstream is validated against
61	  platform needs and documented, with any disqualifying gap escalated back to
62	  the clearance decision.
63	- A midstream repository for the named fallback store exists under
64	  opendatahub-io, mirroring the selected upstream version.
65	- The repository follows the organization's conventions for midstream components.
66	
67	## HLR Traceability
