35	# Productize the fallback object store image with upgrade lifecycle
36	
37	## Description
38	
39	Productizes the Apache-2.0 fallback object store as the supported bundled store
40	image: platform image-hardening standards, a version/upgrade policy, and a
41	published pinned digest for the Platform Operator's enablement configuration.
42	This is the restarted productization the strategy's open question anticipates
43	when the AGPL candidate cannot be distributed. Runs after the midstream
44	repository exists and license validation passes, in parallel with the Konflux
45	onboarding.
46	
47	## Scope
48	
49	- Productized fallback store container image meeting platform image-hardening
50	  standards.
51	- Verification that the fallback store's S3-compatibility behavior meets the
52	  platform's needs (pipelines artifacts and model serving storage).
53	- Version and upgrade policy: new upstream versions flow into the midstream
54	  repository and through the build pipeline without manual rebuild
55	  orchestration.
56	- Publish the pinned image digest for consumption by the Platform Operator
57	  enablement packaging (a configuration reference filled in at execution time).
58	
59	## Acceptance Criteria
60	
61	- The productized fallback store image is published and meets platform image
62	  standards.
63	- The fallback store's S3 compatibility is verified against the pipelines and
64	  model serving storage needs.
65	- An upgrade to a new store image version builds and ships through the pipeline
66	  without manual rebuild orchestration.
67	- The build pipeline is green for the image (gates this epic's completion even
68	  though pipeline onboarding runs in parallel).
69	- The pinned digest of the productized image is available for the operator's
70	  enablement configuration.
71	
72	## HLR Traceability
73	
74	- HLR-2 (P0): productized images and upgrade lifecycle for the bundled store.
