25	# Legal clearance for redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0) in the product
26	
27	## Description
28	
29	Resolves the gating legal unknown of this strategy: whether MinIO, licensed
30	AGPL-3.0, can be redistributed in the product's distribution model, and what
31	derivative-work posture applies when the Platform Operator bundles, deploys, and
32	manages it. The documented decision determines which upstream is productized
33	(MinIO, or the Apache-2.0 fallback named in the strategy) and unblocks all
34	shipping work, which the strategy explicitly holds back until clearance.
35	
36	## Scope
37	
38	- Obtain and document a legal determination on redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0)
39	  under the product's distribution model, including any conditions attached to
40	  clearance.
41	- Document the derivative-work posture for operator integration: whether
42	  bundling, deploying, and managing MinIO through the Platform Operator creates
43	  obligations beyond plain redistribution.
44	- Record a go/no-go per candidate store; on a no-go for MinIO, select (or reject
45	  with rationale) the Apache-2.0 fallback candidate (e.g. SeaweedFS) named in the
46	  strategy's open question. The decision record names the specific upstream to be
47	  productized, so the fallback branch starts with a fixed target for repo
48	  onboarding and license scanning.
49	- Communicate the outcome and the selected upstream to all downstream teams.
50	
51	## Acceptance Criteria
52	
53	- A documented legal determination exists stating whether MinIO (AGPL-3.0) can be
54	  redistributed under the product's distribution model, including any conditions
55	  attached.
56	- The derivative-work posture for operator integration is documented.
57	- The decision names the specific upstream to be productized (MinIO, or a
58	  specific named Apache-2.0 fallback candidate), or records that no candidate
59	  cleared review.
60	- Downstream teams can proceed without further legal interpretation of the AGPL
61	  question.
62	
63	## HLR Traceability
64	
65	- HLR-1 (P0): legal review of redistributing the candidate object store (MinIO,
66	  AGPL-3.0) completed and documented, including the derivative-work posture for
