34	# Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store
35	
36	## Description
37	
38	Delivers the administrator-facing enablement of a supported, bundled S3-compatible
39	object store through the Platform Operator, with productized images and a managed
40	upgrade lifecycle, targeting disconnected and PoC clusters where no
41	customer-provided object storage exists. This epic is upstream-agnostic: it
42	enablements whichever store the legal clearance selects, and consumes the
43	productized store image as a configuration reference (pinned digest) rather than
44	building against it.
45	
46	## Scope
47	
48	- Add an enablement path in the Platform Operator so administrators can turn the
49	  bundled S3-compatible store on through operator configuration, with no external
50	  network access required (disconnected installs).
51	- Deploy and manage the store using the productized store image, referenced by
52	  pinned digest; the digest is filled in at execution time once the productized
53	  image is published.
54	- Manage the upgrade lifecycle: platform upgrades must not orphan or break an
55	  enabled bundled store.
56	- Provide a disable/rollback path so administrators can turn the bundled store off
57	  and fall back to customer-provided storage configuration — the supported
58	  replacement for the ad-hoc, unsupported upstream MinIO installs field teams
59	  perform today.
60	
61	## Acceptance Criteria
62	
63	- On a disconnected cluster, an administrator can enable the bundled S3-compatible
64	  store through Platform Operator configuration with no external network access.
65	- The enabled store runs the productized image referenced by a pinned digest, and
66	  that digest is available at execution time.
67	- A platform upgrade on a cluster with the bundled store enabled completes without
68	  breaking the store or requiring manual reconfiguration.
69	- Administrators can disable the bundled store, with components falling back to
70	  customer-provided storage configuration.
71	
72	## HLR Traceability
73	
74	- HLR-2 (P0): administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object
75	  store through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade
76	  lifecycle.
